        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix embedded compaction hook reset API",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Replaces the proposed arbitrary-key hook reset API with a current-session-scoped `ctx.api.resetSession(reason?)` request.\n- Defers hook-requested resets until the owning lifecycle has left hook dispatch / embedded-run execution, avoiding the active-run self-wait path in the gateway reset service.\n- Wires the deferred reset queue through run-level hooks, direct compaction after-hooks, and queued/context-engine-owned after-compaction hooks.\n- Adds regression coverage for deferred execution, current-session binding, and overflow compaction hook API availability.\n\n## Hatched egg / behavior evidence\n\nThis is an OpenClaw core lifecycle fix, not a Remnic property-data fix. Remnic/context compaction exposed the symptom, but the bug was in the embedded-agent hook/session reset boundary.\n\nBefore this revision, the hook API called `performGatewaySessionReset(...)` synchronously from inside an awaited hook and accepted a caller-supplied key. That could make an after-compaction hook abort and wait on its own active embedded run, and it allowed a hook for one session to target another session key.\n\nAfter this revision:\n\n```ts\nawait hookContext.api.resetSession(\"new\")\nexpect(performGatewaySessionResetMock).not.toHaveBeenCalled()\n```\n\nThe hook call only queues the current session reset while hook code is still executing. The lifecycle owner later drains the queue with trusted metadata:\n\n```ts\nexpect(performGatewaySessionResetMock).toHaveBeenCalledWith({\n  key: \"agent:main:session-1\",\n  agentId: \"main\",\n  reason: \"new\",\n  commandSource: \"embedded-agent:hook\",\n})\n```\n\nCross-session targeting is no longer part of the API. The regression test also proves a string that used to be interpreted as an arbitrary session key is rejected as an invalid reason:\n\n```ts\nawait expect(\n  hookContext.api.resetSession(\"agent:other-session\" as \"reset\"),\n).rejects.toThrow(/reason \"new\" or \"reset\"/)\n```\n\n## Evidence / validation\n\nRebased onto `origin/main` at `9f5609382b5` and pushed as `381aa5f2e88`.\n\n```text\n$ node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.agents-embedded-agent.config.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/compact.hooks.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run.overflow-compaction.test.ts\n\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\nTests       175 passed (175)\n```\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core-pr-compaction-hook-api.tsbuildinfo\n# passed\n```\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.agents.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core-test-agents-pr-compaction-hook-api.tsbuildinfo\n# passed\n```\n\n```text\n$ git diff --check\n# passed\n```\n",
